     "lead": 1.65,
     "align": 0,
     "value": "Robert was born in the spring of 1938 in Fairview, the youngest of four. After serving in the U.S. Navy, he came home to marry his high-school sweetheart, Margaret, and spent thirty-eight years as a machinist at Fairview Tool & Die.\n\nHe coached Little League for two decades, never missed a Sunday service, and could fix nearly anything with a screwdriver and some patience.\n\nHe is survived by Margaret, his children Anna, James and Thomas, seven grandchildren and two great-grandchildren."
